# Start a mission. CANONICAL OWNER: dyx3_mission.
#
# ExecuteMission.action is the canonical mission-execution interface (goal =
# start, feedback = progress, result = outcome, cancel = abort). This service is
# a thin admission-only convenience over the SAME dyx3_mission entry point. Both
# resolve to one code path inside dyx3_mission; no other package may implement either.
#
# 0.15.0 (mission contract v2): ASYNCHRONOUS. The call only admits or refuses (no file I/O, no
# hashing, no PX4 call inside it) and returns the execution id (mission_id). Loading, frame
# placement, arming and OFFBOARD then run in dyx3_mission and are reported on MissionState
# (LOADING -> PLACING -> ARMING -> ENGAGING -> READY -> RUNNING). A missing or corrupt artifact is
# therefore an accepted start that ends in ERROR(PATH_ERROR), not a refusal.

# Content-addressed path artifact produced by the backend (64 lowercase hex).
string path_artifact_sha256
# 0.15.0: optional client request id (idempotency key; 1 to 64 characters of
# [A-Za-z0-9._:-]). A start carrying the request_id of the most recent execution returns that
# execution's mission_id with duplicate = true and starts nothing. Empty = no idempotency.
string request_id
---
bool accepted
uint8 REASON_OK=0
# Malformed artifact id (not 64 lowercase hex). No execution is created.
uint8 REASON_INVALID_ARTIFACT=1
# An execution is active, or the previous one is still releasing OFFBOARD / disarming.
uint8 REASON_BUSY=2
# The guard's pre-arm gate (SafetyGateStatus.pre_arm_ok) is not fresh and ok; see gate_reason_code.
uint8 REASON_SAFETY_GATE=3
# 0.15.0: request_id longer than 64 characters or with characters outside [A-Za-z0-9._:-].
uint8 REASON_INVALID_REQUEST=4
uint8 reason_code
# The execution id: incremented on every accepted start (per process).
uint32 mission_id
# --- appended in 0.15.0 ---
# true: request_id matched the most recent execution; nothing new was started.
bool duplicate
# With REASON_SAFETY_GATE: the guard's first failing pre-arm gate (MotionSetpointStatus.REASON_*;
# REASON_STALE when no fresh SafetyGateStatus). 0 otherwise.
uint8 gate_reason_code
